# Browser test-pass scratch (Playwright artifacts + snapshots) — not part of the app
/.playwright-mcp/
/flow*.png
/flow*.md

# ⚠️ THE SCRATCH DIRECTORY — one rule that retires the whole verification-capture category.
# Per-prefix ignores below were whack-a-mole: every pass invents a prefix no rule anticipates, and it
# either litters `git status` or gets swept into a commit by a `git add -A` (commit 3104918 did exactly
# that to 18 captures). Captures now go to `.captures/` — see .captures/README.md for the convention.
# ⚠️ THE CONTENTS, not the directory. Excluding `/.captures/` outright makes git skip the directory
# entirely, so a `!` negation inside it can never match and the convention doc silently would not ship.
/.captures/*
!/.captures/README.md

# ⚠️ THE BACKSTOP, for when the convention is forgotten: a screenshot with a bare relative filename lands
# at the REPO ROOT, so ignore root-level images outright. This canNOT hide the ~80 root captures already
# committed — a .gitignore rule has no effect on a tracked file — it only stops NEW ones appearing.
# A root image that genuinely belongs in the repo can still be added with `git add -f`.
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.webp
# Dev before/after capture pairs dropped at the repo root during verification passes.
# ⚠️ ROOT-ANCHORED, like /flow*.png above: four before/after images ARE committed assets
# (doemail1-plates, doemail3-admin-email, doinv4-email-plates, email-footer). Git ignores
# never apply to already-tracked paths, so those are unaffected either way — but anchoring
# keeps this rule aimed at the scratch location rather than the filename everywhere.
/*-before-after.png

# Design source: version the .md specs (CATALOGUE + design-system + owner-portal) as the
# source-of-truth; keep the bulky raw Claude Design HTML exports OUT (104MB of self-unpacking
# bundles, regeneratable) — they are referenced by path, not committed.
/docs/design/raw/
/docs/design/*.html

# ⚠️ ENCRYPTED DATABASE + FILE BACKUPS — NEVER commit these. They contain the whole tenant dataset,
# including guest PII and the encrypted ID-document blobs. They are encrypted at rest, but committing
# one would put every customer's data into the repository's history permanently, where a later
# APP_KEY or passphrase leak would expose it retroactively. `storage/` is not wholly ignored here, so
# this directory needs its own rule — it was untracked-but-committable until §7.1 added this line.
/storage/backups/

# Laravel Passport OAuth signing keys — NEVER commit the private key
/storage/oauth-private.key
/storage/oauth-public.key

# Gated build browser-verification screenshots (not part of the regression net)
gate*.png

# The marketing converter's DERIVED input — regenerate with tools/marketing/decode.js from
# docs/design/front/*.dc.html. Not committed: it would be a second copy of the masters (§N.8f).
/tools/marketing/core/

# Local MCP server config — machine-specific paths; must never carry a secret into git.
.mcp.json

# dompdf font metrics, written on first use of a bundled script font (PdfFonts::prepare)
/storage/fonts
